# Comparison table

table = Option,Setup effort,Alerting,Log search,Lock-in,Annual cost; Datadog,low,excellent,excellent,high,"$412,000"; Grafana Cloud,low,good,good,medium,"$236,000"; Self-hosted,high,good,fair,low,"$148,000 + 1.5 engineers"

Self-hosted means Prometheus, Loki and Grafana on our own Kubernetes.

# Three-year cost

data threeyr = year,Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted; 2027,412,236,418; 2028,865,496,706; 2029,1363,782,1004
chart line threeyr x=year y=Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted unit=k$ focus=Grafana Cloud title="Cumulative cost, thousands of dollars"

Self-hosted figures include staff time for 1.5 engineers. Counted that way, Grafana Cloud stays the cheapest in every year.

# Pros and cons

### Datadog
- Pro: excellent alerting and log search.
- Pro: low setup effort.
- Con: highest cost, $1.36M over three years.
- Con: high lock-in.

### Grafana Cloud
- Pro: lowest three-year cost.
- Pro: dashboards stay portable.
- Con: log search is good, not excellent.

### Self-hosted
- Pro: lowest lock-in.
- Pro: lowest license cost.
- Con: high setup effort and fair log search.
- Con: needs 1.5 more engineers.

# Recommendation

! Choose **Grafana Cloud**. It is the cheapest option once staff time is counted, and it keeps our dashboards portable.

! The Datadog quote expires on 2026-11-30. The Self-hosted figures assume we can hire 1.5 engineers, which is not yet approved.
